<title>ITALY: IMF puts Italy lira into currency pool for credits.</title>
<headline>IMF puts Italy lira into currency pool for credits.</headline>
<dateline>ROME 1996-12-05</dateline>
<text>
<p>The board of the International Monetary Fund (IMF) has decided to reinsert the Italian lira into its &quot;operational budget&quot;, the pool of currencies used for credits to member countries, the Italian Treasury said.</p>
<p>The Treasury said the lira had been excluded from the pool since 1992, following its exit from Europe's exchange rate mechanism.  </p>
<p>The lira was reinstated in the ERM at the end of November after floating freely for four years.</p>
<p>&quot;The Fund's decision follows on from the return of the lira to the exchange rate mechanism,&quot; a statement from the Treasury said.</p>
<p>It said the announcement of the lira's reinstatement into the pool had come from the IMF on Thursday.</p>
<p>--Milan bureau +392 66129507</p>
</text>
